{
  "title": "Mock OpenRouter responses poison the shared AI cache",
  "description": "The real AI cache (~/.ramekin/ai-cache) contains hundreds of \
responses that came from tests/mock_openrouter.py rather than the real \
provider: descriptions like \"A delicious test recipe.\", normalize-title \
responses that echo the input title, and mock auto-tags. They are identifiable \
by the mock's fixed usage fingerprint (prompt_tokens: 10, completion_tokens: \
5, total_tokens: 15); a scan on 2026-06-11 found 916 such entries, written \
around 2026-05-18 to 2026-05-26. Something ran the pipeline (or another \
enrichment path) with the AI base URL pointed at the mock server while using \
the default cache dir, so mock output was cached under the real model name \
(google/gemini-2.5-flash).\n\
\n\
Impact: any pipeline run whose enrichment inputs hash to one of the poisoned \
keys silently gets mock data in committed snapshots (e.g. description \"A \
delicious test recipe.\"). This bit the Dotdash ingredient-supplementation \
work on 2026-06-11: changed ingredient lists produced cache keys that collided \
with poisoned entries from a prior run of the same idea.\n\
\n\
Suggested fixes:\n\
1. Purge the poisoned entries (delete cache files whose usage is exactly \
10/5/15).\n\
2. Prevent recurrence: when RAMEKIN_AI_BASE_URL points at a mock/localhost, \
use a separate cache dir (or disable the cache), e.g. derive the cache \
namespace from the base URL the way it is already derived from the model.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
